---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SupportArticle from "../../components/infopages/SupportArticle.astro";
---
<BaseLayout>
  <SupportArticle path="/support/duplicate-a-product" title="Duplicate a product you already have" intro="Own the same lipstick in three shades? Add the first one, then duplicate it for the rest. 💄">

    <h2>Duplicate a product</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open the product in BeautyMark.</li>
      <li>Tap the <strong>•••</strong> button at the top right and choose <strong>Duplicate</strong>.</li>
      <li>A copy opens, ready to edit, with the same brand, name, photo and details. Change the shade (and the photo, if you like).</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Save</strong> (the ✓ on iOS 26 and later).</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The original product isn't changed.</p>

    <h2>Bought the same product again?</h2>
    <p> You don't need a duplicate to remember a repurchase. With <a href="/#pricing">BeautyMark Pro</a>, open the product, tap <strong>•••</strong> then <strong>Edit</strong>, go to the <strong>Advanced</strong> tab, and tap <strong>+ New purchase date</strong>. BeautyMark keeps track of how many times you've bought it.
    </p>
  </SupportArticle>
</BaseLayout>
